"""ant-module-variability — per-(dataset × catalog × module × tag) variability.

Compute the same long-format aggregate parquet as the legacy tool but with:

  * Per-(dataset, catalog) parquet cache under
    ``<h5adstore>/_module_variability_cache/<db_id>/<catalog>.parquet``.
    Invalidated by mtime comparison against the source
    ``.scores.parquet`` sidecar (or the legacy obs-column source: the
    ``.duckdb`` file's mtime).
  * ``multiprocessing.Pool`` over the (dataset × catalog) queue.
    Default ``min(8, cpu_count() // 2)``, override with ``--workers``.
  * ``tqdm`` progress + JSON progress lines to stderr every 10 pairs.
  * Streaming aggregate write via ``duckdb.COPY`` over the cache
    directory — never holds >1 dataset's worth of data in RAM.

Output schema (unchanged):

  ``dataset, source, catalog, module, tag_column, tag, statistic,
    value, n_cells, n_categories``

Statistics per (module × tag × statistic):

  * η² (eta squared) — fraction of module-score variance explained by
    the tag categories. Categorical tags only. [0,1].
  * ω² (omega squared) — bias-corrected η².
  * R² — Pearson² for numerical tags.
  * spearman ρ — signed monotone association for numerical tags.
  * mean_range — max group mean minus min group mean (categorical).
  * total_var — Var(score) on this dataset. Denominator.
  * mean_score — sanity denominator.

Scope: bulk datasets (technology bulk, or about one observation per donor)
are skipped, because there are no cells to describe; the skipped datasets and
the reason are recorded next to the aggregate in
``module_variability.skipped.json`` (see ``lib/cell_level_scope.py``) and
served by ``GET /module-variability``. Donor columns are always categorical.

Usage:
  ant-module-variability [--only DB1,DB2,...] [--tags sex,braak,cluster,...]
                         [--out PATH] [--dry-run] [--force]
                         [--workers N] [--h5adstore-root DIR]
"""
